{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Brothers From Different Mothers feels like a natural follow-up to The New Old Fashioned because close vocal harmonies are what I want to hear now.",
    "Jersey Boys appeals through vocal harmonies, and Nat King Cole's warm singing also interests me, although neither gives me enough reason to choose it today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Guess Who collection, the Peaches & Herb collection, and the banjo-focused album offer different listening experiences from the vocal harmonies I currently want.",
    "Lullaby suggests a bedtime purpose I do not have, while Partners and Album Number Two give me too little information to connect them to my interests."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat older music and familiar performers as enough of a connection, when the singing style matters more to me.",
    "A gentle or comforting mood alone is not enough; enjoying Christmas albums does not mean I am looking for bedtime music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent interaction with The New Old Fashioned is a stronger clue to what I want now: close vocal harmonies.",
    "My Christmas listening was clustered together much earlier, so I would not assume that holiday music is still my main interest. I rarely choose something unless the connection feels clear."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "Some choices captured my interest in warm vocals and harmonies, but many stretched that interest into music with too little connection to what I want now."
}"}
